{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall say to them.</b> A warning to the court. <b>This is the fire-offering,</b> it should have said 'this is the sacrifice,' in keeping with the opening 'My sacrifice'; but he clarifies: 'My bread for My fire-offerings.' <b>To HaShem,</b> for the need of HaShem — that it not become piggul. <b>Lambs.</b> And not other beasts. <b>Of the first year,</b> not a day or an hour more. <b>Without blemish,</b> as it is said (Leviticus 22:21): ״כל מום לא יהיה בו״. תמימם is written deficient (חסר) in yod, to indicate that both of them should be equal. And they are seven hundred and thirty lambs per year, which is three hundred and sixty-five days per year, and twice three hundred and sixty-five is 730, and this is alluded to in the word ת״מימם ש׳נים ל׳יום as an acrostic of the initial letters. <b>Two for each day,</b> they are advocates, intercessors on behalf of Israel, and they are slaughtered corresponding to the day. <b>A continual burnt-offering,</b> this burnt-offering is to be a continual intercessor standing upright on behalf of Israel. <b>For each day</b> — as the day ascends he would say 'bar barqai,' and for this reason 'burnt-offering' (עולה) is not mentioned in the section ואתה תצוה, to be expounded."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The abbreviation תש״ל is expanded as 730 per the surrounding arithmetic context; the acrostic note reads the letters of תמימם plus שנים ליום as ת״מימם ש׳נים ל׳יום. 'ברק ברקאי' (bar barqai) is left untranslated as it appears to be a technical or Aramaic liturgical expression whose precise sense is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:42.694452261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}